280
00:14:42,671 --> 00:14:44,251
And since his crew will be dumbstruck

281
00:14:44,251 --> 00:14:45,571
when they lose their precious boss,

282
00:14:45,571 --> 00:14:48,511
we'll stomp him no problem and claim Chopper in round three.

283
00:14:48,511 --> 00:14:51,051
Then we're guaranteed to keep him for good, get it?

284
00:14:54,071 --> 00:14:56,331
No, say it isn't so!

285
00:14:56,331 --> 00:14:59,091
They're really gonna take our captain away?

286
00:14:59,091 --> 00:15:01,571
But that's the peanut strategy!

287
00:15:01,571 --> 00:15:03,831
You guys are the lowest of the low!

288
00:15:03,831 --> 00:15:06,371
Go home, lousy peanuters!

289
00:15:06,371 --> 00:15:08,931
Are you afraid to fight us fair?

290
00:15:08,931 --> 00:15:11,251
Although there's no rule against this strategy,

291
00:15:11,251 --> 00:15:13,391
it certainly seems a bit underhanded.

292
00:15:13,391 --> 00:15:15,511
A little cheating is expected of pirates,

293
00:15:15,511 --> 00:15:17,431
but suddenly taking a crew's captain away

294
00:15:17,431 --> 00:15:18,291
in the middle of a game

295
00:15:18,291 --> 00:15:20,411
is no different than running from a fight.

296
00:15:20,411 --> 00:15:23,091
Shame, shame on you straw hats,

297
00:15:23,091 --> 00:15:24,831
and shame on the heartless devil of a woman

298
00:15:24,831 --> 00:15:26,391
who came up with this plan.

299
00:15:26,391 --> 00:15:29,831
You're truly a nefarious navigator, Nami!

300
00:15:29,831 --> 00:15:32,211
How dare you talk trash about Nami!

301
00:15:32,211 --> 00:15:33,591
I ought to fillet you punks!

302
00:15:33,591 --> 00:15:35,751
In the long history of Davy Black fights,

303
00:15:35,751 --> 00:15:37,451
no one has ever had the audacity

304
00:15:37,451 --> 00:15:39,791
to pull such a lousy, no-good stunt.

305
00:15:39,791 --> 00:15:41,211
So what do you say, men?

306
00:15:41,211 --> 00:15:42,831
You can't call a win against the crew

307
00:15:42,831 --> 00:15:45,631
with no captain of true victory, can you?

308
00:15:45,631 --> 00:15:46,791
No!

309
00:15:46,791 --> 00:15:48,951
after swearing on Davy Jones' name,

310
00:15:48,951 --> 00:15:51,171
is it right to throw away your honor as a pirate

311
00:15:51,171 --> 00:15:52,931
just to win a match?!

312
00:15:52,931 --> 00:15:54,111
No!

313
00:15:54,111 --> 00:15:55,291
Ha ha ha!

314
00:15:55,291 --> 00:15:56,971
Why are they so mean?

315
00:15:56,971 --> 00:15:59,371
Well, even if it doesn't go against the rules,

316
00:15:59,371 --> 00:16:02,211
it does seem to go against some of their pirate sensibilities.

317
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:04,811
Peanuts! Peanuts! Peanuts!

318
00:16:04,811 --> 00:16:08,391
Shut up! You guys are making me mad!

319
00:16:08,391 --> 00:16:10,391
I'm with Nami on this one!

320
00:16:10,391 --> 00:16:12,631
I don't know. I think they're right.

321
00:16:12,631 --> 00:16:14,691
Nami, why don't you grow a backbone?

322
00:16:14,691 --> 00:16:17,551
You're just making a big fuss because you lost!

323
00:16:17,551 --> 00:16:19,391
How about you shut up and deal with it?

324
00:16:19,391 --> 00:16:20,891
Yes, ma'am, we're sorry!

325
00:16:20,891 --> 00:16:23,731
Underhanded witch, though she is, the girl is right.

326
00:16:23,731 --> 00:16:26,071
Monkey D. Loopy is the captain of the winning team,

327
00:16:26,071 --> 00:16:28,871
so it's up to him to decide how this battle will unfold.

328
00:16:28,871 --> 00:16:31,871
That is to say, he's free to choose anyone he likes,

329
00:16:31,871 --> 00:16:33,831
including Foxy himself!

330
00:16:33,831 --> 00:16:34,711
This is it.

331
00:16:34,711 --> 00:16:36,271
He's picking me for sure.

332
00:16:36,271 --> 00:16:37,551
It's not so bad.

333
00:16:37,551 --> 00:16:40,251
I'm sure I'll have fun sailing with them.

334
00:16:40,251 --> 00:16:41,711
No matter how you slice it,

335
00:16:41,711 --> 00:16:44,051
I'm the only choice that makes sense.

336
00:16:44,051 --> 00:16:45,411
Oh, look at me!

337
00:16:45,411 --> 00:16:46,311
Please!

338
00:16:46,311 --> 00:16:48,691
I know I'm handsome, but I don't want to go!

339
00:16:48,691 --> 00:16:50,751
So they're gonna pick me, huh?

340
00:16:50,751 --> 00:16:52,551
I knew these guys were cool.

341
00:16:52,551 --> 00:16:54,331
Can I leave my friends behind?

342
00:16:54,331 --> 00:16:56,231
How will they go on without me?

343
00:16:56,231 --> 00:16:57,131
Oh, no!

344
00:16:57,131 --> 00:16:59,431
How is Foxy ever gonna replace me?

345
00:16:59,431 --> 00:17:02,371
Straw-head, you little punk!

346
00:17:09,711 --> 00:17:12,111
You're really going to choose me, aren't you?

347
00:17:12,111 --> 00:17:13,671
Yes, it's obvious.

348
00:17:13,671 --> 00:17:16,651
That was probably your plan all along.

349
00:17:16,651 --> 00:17:18,651
Farewell, Foxy Pirates.

350
00:17:18,651 --> 00:17:20,831
Farewell, my wonderful crew.

351
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:23,131
I'll say goodbye with a smile on my face.

352
00:17:23,131 --> 00:17:25,231
I owe you that much, at least.

353
00:17:25,231 --> 00:17:27,431
If having such a charming personality

354
00:17:27,431 --> 00:17:29,091
and stunning looks is a sin,

355
00:17:29,091 --> 00:17:30,891
then I accept my punishment.

356
00:17:30,891 --> 00:17:33,931
Those poor straw hats really need a poster boy for their crew.

357
00:17:33,931 --> 00:17:35,371
I can't blame them for wanting me.

358
00:17:35,371 --> 00:17:37,711
I can't blame anyone for wanting me.

359
00:17:37,711 --> 00:17:39,811
Say, just a quick thought.

360
00:17:39,811 --> 00:17:41,011
That plan of yours,

361
00:17:41,011 --> 00:17:43,011
although it would give us a big advantage,

362
00:17:43,011 --> 00:17:46,251
you realize it would also make Foxy a part of our crew.

363
00:17:46,251 --> 00:17:47,351
Uh...

364
00:17:47,351 --> 00:17:48,851
Yeah, I think I'll pass.

365
00:17:48,851 --> 00:17:50,851
Oh!

366
00:17:53,731 --> 00:17:54,391
Oh!

367
00:17:54,391 --> 00:17:56,151
Our sweet captain's heart has been crushed

368
00:17:56,151 --> 00:17:57,891
under the weight of those cruel words!

369
00:17:57,891 --> 00:17:59,331
It's one thing to turn him down,

370
00:17:59,331 --> 00:18:01,071
but did they have to do it like that?

371
00:18:01,071 --> 00:18:01,871
Aw!

372
00:18:01,871 --> 00:18:02,831
It's okay!

373
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:05,171
Even if they don't want you, we still do!

374
00:18:05,171 --> 00:18:06,831
You're always welcome here!

375
00:18:06,831 --> 00:18:09,031
Do you mean it?

376
00:18:09,031 --> 00:18:11,471
Nobody makes fun of our boss and gets away with it!

377
00:18:11,471 --> 00:18:12,571
Yeah, you'll see!

378
00:18:12,571 --> 00:18:13,811
We'll get him next round!

379
00:18:13,811 --> 00:18:15,071
We won't let you down, boss!

380
00:18:15,071 --> 00:18:15,871
I promise!

381
00:18:15,871 --> 00:18:16,811
We love you!

382
00:18:17,811 --> 00:18:18,711
You're leaving!

383
00:18:18,711 --> 00:18:19,911
You guys!

384
00:18:19,911 --> 00:18:20,971
Thank you!

385
00:18:20,971 --> 00:18:22,951
I promise I'll never leave!

386
00:18:22,951 --> 00:18:25,271
You're the only crew for me!

387
00:18:25,271 --> 00:18:26,551
Cut the crap, will ya?

388
00:18:28,951 --> 00:18:32,191
Now that the straw hats are done emotionally abusing our boss,

389
00:18:32,191 --> 00:18:34,751
it's time for them to make their decision!

390
00:18:34,751 --> 00:18:35,491
Come on!

391
00:18:35,491 --> 00:18:37,751
Don't leave us in suspense any longer!

392
00:18:39,031 --> 00:18:41,031
Fine!

393
00:18:41,031 --> 00:18:45,031
In that case, there's someone I want to take back!

394
00:18:45,031 --> 00:18:46,031
Shelly!

395
00:18:46,031 --> 00:18:47,031
Huh?

396
00:18:47,031 --> 00:18:48,031
What a turn of events!

397
00:18:48,031 --> 00:18:49,031
The captain of the straw hats has chosen Shelly,

398
00:18:49,031 --> 00:18:50,031
